# ============================================================================
# SAWO.COM RESPONSE HEADERS — Cloudflare Pages format
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ported from the old frontend/vercel.json (Vercel-only config, never read by
# Cloudflare Pages — the site's actual deploy target). vercel.json's rewrites
# were removed for good (they pointed at the abandoned Next.js app), but
# these headers were real, live behavior with no Cloudflare-native home until
# now, so they're carried over as-is rather than dropped.
#
# Cloudflare Pages auto-discovers a file named exactly `_headers` in the
# build output root (CRA copies public/ into build/ unchanged, so this file
# living in public/ is sufficient — same convention as _redirects).
# Docs: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
#
# Syntax: a path pattern on its own line, followed by indented header lines
# that apply to it. First-match-wins does NOT apply here the way it does in
# _redirects — Cloudflare merges headers from every matching block, more
# specific paths first.
# ============================================================================

/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.webp
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-XSS-Protection: 1; mode=block
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
